      "message": "So not necessarily.  I think we can allow a \"cloud admin\" (as shown in policy.v3cloudsample.json) access to the grant APIs (since those should not need to access identity) - provided our policy building code just ignores and users/groups it can\u0027t find (since they may be in a different domain).  Given that, a cloud admin can grant themselves a role on a domain in which they want to do user and group management...and then get domain_scoped token on that domain to do it.  Not perfect, but workable.  Such an approach would not open up cross domain security issues for domain admins, since non-cloud admins would still only be able to grant roles on their domain.",
